                <pb facs="0593" n="558" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v29/pg558"/>

                <head>226. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Brzezinski) to Secretary of State Vance, Secretary of the Treasury Blumenthal,
                    Secretary of Commerce Kreps, and the Special Representative for Trade
                    Negotiations (Strauss)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d226-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1979-05-15">May 15, 1979</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item> U.S. Investment Team to Panama</item>
                </list>
                <p>In his meeting with Panamanian President Royo, on May 10, 1979,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d226-f2"/> President Carter agreed to Royo’s suggestion that the
                    U.S. government send a high-level team to Panama to encourage U.S. investment
                    and trade with that country. Both Presidents referred to the Strauss Mission to
                    Egypt and Israel as an example of the kind of mission the U.S. should <pb
                        facs="0594" n="559" xml:id="pg559"/> send to Panama.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d226-f3"/> The State Department should coordinate this effort with
                    agencies in the government, interested Members of Congress, the U.S. business
                    community, and the Panamanian government. Please report as appropriate.<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d226-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Zbigniew Brzezinski</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
